      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Labeled maximum:** The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Single doses are usually capped at 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose:** tell me the dose and frequency you want\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm it explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that the dose was intentional."
      }
